From faa94d3740a1af56e19b587a9df851c0418e0b2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 19:09:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Fix verification pipeline reliability and remove
 fabricated evidence

Nine defects found by reading and running the pipeline, grouped by what
they affected.

Silent failure of the ML worker
- /api/health returned a static "ok" no matter what was running, including
  the failure that broke verification most often: the Python worker not
  being started. It now probes the database and the worker and returns 503
  when a decision-critical dependency is down. Missing LLM keys never fail
  the check, since Layer 5 is enhancement-only.
- Added a /health route to ai_server.py reporting per-model load state.
  FastAPI serves /openapi.json regardless, so the old reachability probe
  treated a worker with no models loaded as healthy.
- Added a boot-time self-check so a missing worker is visible at startup.
- Centralised every ML call in services/ml_client.js: one configurable base
  URL, explicit IPv4 loopback (localhost resolves to ::1 first on many
  machines while uvicorn binds IPv4, surfacing as "fetch failed"), and
  timeouts on every request so a hung worker cannot hold Express open.
- Documented the worker as a required startup step in the README, which
  previously omitted it entirely.

Fabricated or discarded evidence
- checkModelProportions overwrote the detected model height with a
  hardcoded "tall (5'8+)" for kurtis and dresses, then compared the seller's
  declaration against that invented value and returned it to the UI as
  "detected". Removed; it also mutated the caller's object.
- Layer 4 was skipped entirely whenever CLIP was unavailable, discarding
  valid pHash and attribute evidence and reporting no score. Fusion now runs
  on whatever signals exist and reports confidence_tier, signals_used and
  signals_missing; a prior-only result is suppressed rather than shown as a
  measurement.
- The UI added 15 percentage points per "resolved" row directly to the
  Bayesian posterior. Because probability arrives as a string it was doing
  string concatenation, so the number shown was neither the model's nor the
  intended boost. Removed in favour of a re-check prompt.
- The UI rendered an unobserved likelihood ratio as "0.00", which reads as
  overwhelming evidence against a match rather than "not measured".

Checks that silently did not run
- analyzeCatalogGeometry keyed the garment mask off a 10-entry hue table,
  so it returned null for every black, white, grey, beige, cream or brown
  garment and skipped the Layer 3.7 length check on a large share of real
  listings. It now falls back to a dominant-foreground-colour mask, reports
  mask_source and mask_confidence, and downgrades low-confidence length
  findings to warnings so a noisier mask cannot block publication.
- CANONICAL_MAP declared 'cap sleeve' twice; the later entry won, so a cap
  sleeve could never match a short-sleeve observation. Also removed a
  duplicate bare 'long' and added full/long as a soft equivalence.

Untrusted input reaching the network and filesystem
- materializeCatalogReferences fetched any seller-supplied URL, including
  cloud metadata and private ranges. Private, loopback, link-local and
  multicast destinations are now refused.
- Its relative-path fallback resolved any client string against the process
  CWD, accepting ../../../../etc/passwd as a catalog image. Local reads are
  now confined to the allowed asset roots.
- A request whose references were all rejected returned a generic "upload
  catalog images" error; it now says which reference failed and why.

Other
- enhanceMetadataWithVision uploaded every anchor as image/jpeg, so PNG
  anchors were rejected or mis-decoded. MIME type now comes from the file.
- test_e2e.js did not load dotenv, so it signed evidence bindings with the
  fallback secret while the server used .env, failing every recheck test.
  Its health assertion hardcoded 200, which would have passed in exactly the
  situation the check exists to catch; it now asserts the response shape and
  that the status agrees with the underlying checks.

Verified: test_e2e.js 21/21, test_evidence.js passing, frontend builds,
striped-dress fixture still blocks on catalog visual mismatch, SSRF and
traversal payloads refused, worker-down path returns a specific
EVIDENCE_PENDING reason.

