From d741ab4901596f2ece9887bed73caf6133e2f2b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 21:32:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Redesign the verification results page: one verdict, one
 fix list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Restructures the results page around a simple reading order — what happened,
what to fix, then the evidence — and removes the repetition where the same
issue appeared in three different boxes. Verified in a real browser by driving
the full CSV flow (login -> workflow chooser -> CSV upload -> row select ->
anchor upload -> verification) with Playwright against the kurti fixture.

Verdict hero (replaces the old verdict bar):
- Plain-language headline ("4 issues must be fixed before this listing goes
  live"), status pill, and readable count chips.
- Animated score ring that states its provenance: "Estimated from the stored
  evidence record" for hash-bound fixture results vs "Measured live from your
  images" for general uploads — the estimate/measured distinction was
  previously invisible.

One fix list instead of three overlapping cards:
- The correction co-pilot card and the separate consistency-copilot card
  showed the same issues twice; the copilot's status now folds into the fix
  list header and the duplicate card is gone.
- Each fix item reads: field -> "Your listing says" vs "Evidence shows"
  (strikethrough on the contradicted value) -> why it matters -> how to fix,
  with Apply / Keep-my-value actions. Server suggestions that are
  instructions rather than observed values render only under "How to fix",
  never as fake evidence.
- The evidence-record box and the sticky action bar no longer repeat the
  verdict sentence the hero already shows; the action bar now says how many
  blocking issues remain instead.

Parity for general uploads:
- The live comparison table is re-enabled (it was dead code behind `false &&`)
  with the same "Focus on issues" toggle the fixture matrix has, and an
  all-clear state.
- The raw CLIP-fabric and pHash cards collapse into a single "Measurement
  detail" drawer that also lists the verification-network channels with their
  status and likelihood ratios.

Readability and theme:
- Type floor raised across the page (nothing seller-facing below ~12.5px);
  the workflow-chooser descriptions under the two flow buttons were 12px
  low-contrast grey and are now legible.
- Myntra pink on white carried through hero, chips, fix items and toggles;
  staggered entrance animation with prefers-reduced-motion respected.

The three protected demo fixtures are unaffected (presentation-only change);
the kurti fixture path was re-driven end-to-end in the browser after the
redesign and returns the same verdict, counts and score. Frontend builds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013dH2GRLbUQX4E4mnweV9Bn
